From: A6L port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] hwc: keep the CRTC's display resources across display power-off

On power-off the composer cleared MODE_ID and detached the connector
("teardown"), so the kernel released the CRTC's hardware blocks (msm DPU CTL,
layer mixer, DSPP). On the A6L the e-ink CRTC (a DRM lessee of a6l_epdd) is
then modeset while the LCD is off (lock screen) and the DPU resource manager
hands it the LCD's CTL, whose flush register still holds bits for the LCD
interface that only an LCD vsync can consume: every e-ink commit timed out
("vblank timeout: 41002841" for 7 s on 7 Oct 06:28) and the phone hard-reset.

Power-off now only clears ACTIVE (panel and interface off as before) unless
vendor.hwc.drm.power_off_teardown=1. Power-on re-applies the same mode, which
the kernel treats as an ACTIVE-only change: the resources stay with the LCD.

--- a/hwc/HwcDisplay.cpp
+++ b/hwc/HwcDisplay.cpp
@@ -644,7 +644,17 @@ HwcDisplay::Error HwcDisplay::SetPowerMode(PowerMode mode) {
   a_args.blocking = true;
   a_args.power_mode = mode;
   if (!enabled) {
-    a_args.teardown = true;
+    // A6L (eink-round6): by default only ACTIVE=0 here; MODE_ID and the
+    // connector link stay set, so the kernel keeps this CRTC's display
+    // resources (msm DPU: CTL, LM, DSPP are only re-assigned when the mode or
+    // the connectors change, not when only ACTIVE does). A teardown released
+    // the LCD's CTL with a flush pending for the LCD interface that only the
+    // LCD can consume; the next e-ink modeset (lock screen while asleep) got
+    // that CTL and every e-ink commit then timed out ("vblank timeout:
+    // 41002841", 7 Oct 06:28) until the phone reset. The panel and the
+    // interface are switched off by ACTIVE=0 exactly as before.
+    // vendor.hwc.drm.power_off_teardown=1 restores the upstream teardown.
+    a_args.teardown = Properties::PowerOffTeardown();
   }
 
   const bool commit_success = ExecuteAtomicCommit(a_args).has_value();
--- a/utils/properties.cpp
+++ b/utils/properties.cpp
@@ -185,6 +185,15 @@ auto Properties::LeaseSocketName() -> std::string {
   return {buf};
 }
 
+/**
+ * Display power-off also detaches the connector and clears the mode (true), or
+ * only clears ACTIVE (false, the A6L default: the kernel keeps the CRTC's
+ * hardware blocks reserved for this display, see HwcDisplay::SetPowerMode).
+ */
+auto Properties::PowerOffTeardown() -> bool {
+  return (property_get_bool("vendor.hwc.drm.power_off_teardown", 0) != 0);
+}
+
 auto Properties::DropDrmMasterAfterInit() -> bool {
   return (property_get_bool("ro.vendor.hwc.drop_drm_master", 0) != 0);
 }
--- a/utils/properties.h
+++ b/utils/properties.h
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ class Properties {
   static auto ForceP3Support() -> bool;
   static auto IgnoredConnectors() -> std::string;
   static auto LeaseSocketName() -> std::string;
+  static auto PowerOffTeardown() -> bool;
 };
 
 }  // namespace android::drm_hwcomposer
